From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:41:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/77] Integer constant folding during inline/propagation
 simplification does not report overflow

simplify(forinline=true) runs on inlined bodies and after constant
propagation (-O3). An addition, subtraction or multiplication that
overflows there was not a constant expression in the source, but the
folder reported 'Overflow in arithmetic operation' and rejected valid
code (V0 := 4022060303630; if B then V0 := V0 * V0 at -O3; trunk also
propagates into case-of-string branches). Leave such operations to run
time, where they wrap or raise the overflow check error.
---
 compiler/nadd.pas | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/nadd.pas b/compiler/nadd.pas
index 1758a79e..72a60666 100644
--- a/compiler/nadd.pas
+++ b/compiler/nadd.pas
@@ -830,6 +830,12 @@ const
                    v:=lv+rv;
                    if v.overflow then
                      begin
+                       { when simplifying an inlined body or after constant
+                         propagation, the operation was not a constant
+                         expression in the source: leave it to run time, where
+                         it wraps or raises an overflow check error }
+                       if forinline then
+                         exit;
                        Message(parser_e_arithmetic_operation_overflow);
                        { Recover }
                        t:=genintconstnode(0)
@@ -852,6 +858,12 @@ const
                    v:=lv-rv;
                    if v.overflow then
                      begin
+                       { when simplifying an inlined body or after constant
+                         propagation, the operation was not a constant
+                         expression in the source: leave it to run time, where
+                         it wraps or raises an overflow check error }
+                       if forinline then
+                         exit;
                        Message(parser_e_arithmetic_operation_overflow);
                        { Recover }
                        t:=genintconstnode(0)
@@ -884,6 +896,12 @@ const
                    v:=lv*rv;
                    if v.overflow then
                      begin
+                       { when simplifying an inlined body or after constant
+                         propagation, the operation was not a constant
+                         expression in the source: leave it to run time, where
+                         it wraps or raises an overflow check error }
+                       if forinline then
+                         exit;
                        message(parser_e_arithmetic_operation_overflow);
                        { Recover }
                        t:=genintconstnode(0)
